## F3 · ◇ Decide — cut and build order

One K15 authority/byte lane should define face atom + FCK, place KEL duties, S-row semantics, and old-byte refusal. Implement in dependent slices:

1. **Contracts/bytes first (pre-X0):** face selection, per-face Keyhive Individual/archive/card; explicit refusal of legacy mixed place archive by name; no CRDT document survives until X0, so re-genesis replaces migration. Files: `ceremony-core.ts`, node `init.ts`/`place-card.ts`/`leaf-identity.ts`, browser `open-browser-vessel.ts`/`browser-vessel-identity.ts`/daemon bootstrap. **Identity bytes move here**, before X0: DID/card/archive ownership, gate proof and signature identities change. Reds: place seed cannot mint/open any face card/archive; selected A atom succeeds, B and faceless refuse. Control: independent face archives and cards; no shared archive restoration. Known positive: current face-arm leaf already loads atom/card (`leaf-identity.ts:41-57`), and browser face presentation uses atom (`open-browser-vessel.ts:862-869`).
2. **Floor and carrier edges:** route all floor writers through scoped place signer; remove place ContactCard from general carriage; adjust public floor card and consumers. Patch W14-W16: `place-floor-pin`, `admit-gate-pin`, `hearth-gate-pins`, `herm-carriage`, `nexus-contract`, `carry-bundle`, `browser-gate-pins`, `browser-floor-read`, browser card filing, `main.ts`/`live-status.ts`. Reds: place seed cannot prove a face or sign outside five duties; control checks each duty and refusal outside it. Known positive: current floor-door adapter and floor policy provide seam (`open-node-vessel.ts:713,1375,1505`; census `:17-35`).
3. **Daemon / ports:** consume face atom/FCK only for face daemon proof, with faceless daemon authority absent; port/admission contract follows the same identity boundary. Patch D2: TW5 port/island protocol, hand-gate, projection, web `projection-sink`, node `open-node-vessel` port hunks. Reds: no-face cannot enter private/face worker or open group secret; selected face succeeds. Known positive: browser and node already pass atom separately (`open-browser-vessel.ts:1333-1358`; node `open-node-vessel.ts:2287-2300`).
4. **Relay / carriage cadence:** mint random relay S key, principal and opener explicitly as relay service; persist key and public pin, no face/place derivation. Replace `nodeSeedHex` with public place identifier or local jitter. Patch node `carriage-relay.ts`, herm relay callers, `carriage-caps.ts`. Red: place thief cannot recreate relay; positive: S-row survives restart and carries opaque bytes only. No floor-duty expansion.
5. **Face actions / plugins:** explicit face atom signatures for internal face asks and meme promotion; classify each ask by protected relation, no shared S key. G15 owns `afterRollChain` and `build-plugin-tiddler`; its interface consumes selected-face capability. Red: absent/ambiguous face refuses; positive selected face verifies as itself. G15 follows K15 contract; identity format hunks precede X0.

Run the census as a closure check only after these contracts land; amend it to follow aliases/parameters or keep an explicit handoff ledger. Never let its green token match stand as proof of no seed flow. Three settled points constrain all slices: relay S row names service principal/opener; command names explicit face and refuses ambiguity; internal ask authority follows protected relation per call.

## ▶ Act / ↺ Hoʻoko — operator list and close

**Only surviving operator choice:** which named relay S row/principal/opener and persistence location should the house standardize? Options: (A) node-local random durable S row, relay service principal and relay-only opener; (B) one separately provisioned random S row per relay instance. **Lean A** for one stable service identity across restart, with explicit rotation and no environment-seed fallback. No shared secret, no face link.

No operator question remains on Keyhive identity, ContactCard peer proof, face selection, or internal asks; house law settles them. No tests/suites or git writes. Repository reads only; handback written in this seat.

